    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0257" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/40</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-20">June 20, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received June
                        29.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Embassy’s strictly
                    confidential telegrams No. 158 of June 17, 4 p.m., and No. 159 of June 18, 1
                    p.m., I have the honor to enclose the text of my speech at the dinner given in
                    my honor by The Pilgrims on Tuesday, June 18th, at the Hotel Victoria, London. I
                    am sending the text published in the <hi rendition="#italic">Times</hi> of June
                    19th. The few minor inaccuracies printed have been corrected in ink on each copy
                    forwarded.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray
                            Atherton</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>


                <xi:include href="d78-a1.xml" xpointer="d78-a1"/>
            </div>
